# Story 3: Your First Session (50s)
# Hook: Name your session. Detach. Reattach. Your work is always waiting.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-03-first-session.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 9

[00:00.0 --> 00:02.0]
Name your session. Detach. Reattach. Your work is always waiting.

[00:02.0 --> 00:07.0]
Start rysh with a session name. This creates a persistent workspace.

[00:07.0 --> 00:13.0]
Work as you normally would. Run commands, explore your project.

[00:13.0 --> 00:19.0]
Ctrl+P n splits a pane. Now you have two terminals.

[00:19.0 --> 00:24.0]
Each pane is independent. Run different tasks side by side.

[00:24.0 --> 00:30.0]
Ctrl+O enters prefix mode. Press d to detach. You're back at your original shell, but the session lives on.

[00:30.0 --> 00:36.0]
List your sessions to see what's running.

[00:36.0 --> 00:44.0]
Reattach and everything is exactly where you left it. Your panes, your output, your context -- all preserved.

[00:44.0 --> 00:50.0]
Both panes are still here. Pick up right where you left off.

